            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0555" n="487" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg487"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11 Se 8/53½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">12 October, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I entirely approve of
                    this.</p>
                <p>I notice that there is nothing in the despatch to intimate to the Imperial
                    Government that the submission to arbitration will need, so far as we are
                    concerned, the consent of the Senate. Would it not be well to instruct the
                    Ambassador to give this information to the Berlin Foreign Office?</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
